Rung T writes the static numerals into the specification in the revision form, replacing climb batch 29's field numerals, and it is right as the section asks. I checked every passage and box against P-174, P-176, P-173, P-40, P-165, P-37, P-96, the snapshot's sections 2, 3, 5 and 11, forks A1-A8 and T1-T3, and the probe's patch and report. What I checked:
- the numeral types and their four numbers;
- the five-trait hierarchy;
- the eleven library coercions and the prelude's seven;
- no = pairs and no asFloat;
- the interval;
- the sign rule;
- the where clause;
- one value per place;
- the written-only rule;
- the binary boxes;
- the constant chapter;
- the entry rewritten in place;
- the rows: closed rows are named nowhere, and 957's second case and 971 are written open.

The report and record were already on the branch, byte-identical to the journal (cmp silent). Only Specification/ and explorations/ change, so no stage could move. There is no test, since the rung is prose. The worker's last build ran on its final text.

My fixes:
1. 05b264bf5c (defect, settled): two Effect sentences said more than holds. The top-level = over Any was claimed for every number type other than the numeral's default, but ZZ64, ZZ, QQ and RR64 declare = at ZZ32. Row 962's sentence took in the four numbers of a numeral type, which are read as ZZ. Line counts are kept. The specification built with both BUILD SUCCESSFUL and 0 warnings.
2. b7a8a42492 (correction): record.md now hands over five moved citations the worker missed: F-272, F-175's second range, F-173's second range, and the dormant-code map's binary and conversions-coercions rows.

The differential programs on old and new code are identical, as they must be for a prose rung. They confirm the constant chapter's examples and the compiled u = 0 true. SKEPTIC.md is committed and pushed, last.
